   "widgets_values": [
    "## Probe: frame interpolation (E17)\n\n**Video in, video out with synthesised in-between frames.** RIFE (`rife_v4.25.safetensors`, 21.6 MB,\nMIT) or FILM (`film_net_fp16.safetensors`, 65.7 MB, Apache-2.0) - both in `models/frame_interpolation/`.\nPick the model on node 3, the factor on node 4.\n\n**The input is deliberately `dance_2x.mp4`** - our frame-duplicated slow-motion build, 242 frames where\nevery second frame is a copy of the one before. If the model interpolates, the frames between those\nduplicates are new; if it merely re-times, they are copies again. That is the measurement.\n\n**`fps` on the last node is the meaning**, because the chain is 1:1 in time and only frame *count* changes:\n\n- `fps` = the clip's own (**24.12** here) -> **slow motion**: 484 frames over ~20 s, now with real\n  in-betweens instead of duplicates;\n- `fps` = **2x** the clip's (**48.24** here) -> **same duration, twice the frames**: the smoother-clip\n  case, ~10 s like the source.\n\nThis is scaffolding for the E17 measurement in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`, not a curated flow: it is\nunmaintained by design (`workflows/scratch/`), and once E17 has a verdict the useful half should be\nfolded into a shipped flow with a story.\n"
   ],
